83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The Shopping Wishlist Manager is a console-based application that helps a user keep track of items they want to buy. The user can add items with prices, display the whole wishlist, sort the items by price, remove an item and view the total cost. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project written in Java as a single .java file and run from the console.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (A singly linked list, built from a Node class that holds the data and a next reference, stores the wishlist records in memory. The sorting logic \(by price, low to high\) and the searching logic \(finding an item by its ID\) are written manually, without any built-in sort or search methods. Item IDs are generated automatically, starting from W101, and removing an item never changes the IDs of the remaining items.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The wishlist is stored in a text file named wishlist.txt. The data is loaded from this file when the program starts and saved back to it when the program exits, so the wishlist is not lost between runs. The project needs no database, no graphical interface and no external library, which keeps the scope suitable for a college-level submission.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
