635 0 obj
<<
/Title (removeItem\(id\) searches the list manually from the head for the matching ID. If found, the node is unlinked by changing the previous node's next reference \(special cases: first node and last node\). Other items keep their IDs. If not found, "Item W999 not found." is printed. totalCost\(\) traverses the list, adds all prices and counts the nodes, then prints "Total wishlist cost: X | Items: N".)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 627 0 R
/Prev 641 0 R
>>
endobj
636 0 obj
<<
/Title (loadFromFile\(\) is called once at the start. It reads each line using BufferedReader, splits it into ID, name and price, builds a Node and adds it to the list. It also finds the highest ID number so that nextId continues correctly.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 613 0 R
/Prev 628 0 R
/Next 637 0 R
>>
endobj
